{
  "comment": "The recorded-invocation gate. Each scenario is one offline invocation: argv, environment, and recorded responses. The stage 1 scenarios were generated by the TypeScript implementation this package replaced and remain the cross-language parity gate (docs/design/v1-python.md \u00a75); the stage 2 host, vuln, and scopes scenarios and the stage 3 NG-SIEM search scenarios are regression pins generated from this implementation. Four stage 1 documents changed at stage 2 (help-top, unknown-command, home-view, home-view-no-credential) because the command surface grew to the one docs/design/v1.md \u00a71.4 specifies, and eight changed at stage 3 (those four plus scopes, auth-status, auth-status-member-cid, auth-status-retargeted) because captain exception N1 added the NG-SIEM search surface and the NGSIEM:write scope it requires (docs/design/v1.md \u00a74.3). help-vuln-list changed when vuln list gained --fields (docs/design/v1.md \u00a710). help-top, unknown-command, home-view, and scopes changed when cve show shipped: the command list, the home suggestion, and the license-gated Falcon Intelligence scope (docs/design/v1.md \u00a72.2).",
